## Finding

The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) calls this one known parser issue. The rendered
evidence separates two causes. The parser ticket cannot resolve the booking form's hint.
This page reassesses the 4 October export, not a live production feed.

## Final disposition · engineering update, 5 October

The course desk has now reported **#4471 closed on 5 October**:

- **Parser: fixed** — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The parser ticket is
  closed as completed.
- **Hint: won't fix** — booking-v3 form retired. The hint ticket is closed as not planned,
  not as a shipped hint fix.

Closure does not mean both defects were repaired. Keep the two causes and their separate
outcomes visible. The computed table below describes the original export's merge state;
its "no ticket of its own" label is historical, not the state of the newly filed GitHub issues.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Separate tickets

- [Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first](https://github.com/kacperborowieckb/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
  The shared parser interprets input month-first for day-first tenants. For example,
  Harbour Dental's R-41200 describes 7 April becoming 4 July. Parse according to the
  declared tenant format; test ambiguous and unambiguous dates through app, email and booking-v2.
- [Booking-v3 date hint contradicts the tenant's parsing order](https://github.com/kacperborowieckb/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
  Its form says `MM/DD/YYYY`, while it reads input using the day-first tenant locale.
  Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour run that form. Generate the hint and
  parser from one locale-aware format. Test form submissions separately from app/email.

Counts above are computed from unique report IDs, filtered to `mergedInto === 4471`.
Export pages overlap; raw rows are not independent reports. Classification calls `causeOf`
with each report's channel and the tenant directory's locale and form version.
Browser locale and intake tags are guesses, not the grouping rule. The table shows their disagreements.

<Callout kind="warn">
The desk's one-day-move notes remain counted under their tenant-derived cause and are
footnoted in the table. A one-day shift does not itself prove a month/day swap. Keep these
reports for reproduction; if evidence establishes another cause, open a separate ticket
and revise the partition rather than silently discarding them.
</Callout>

## What the queue shows

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports arrived before the bulk merge. A later merge date is desk processing, not the bug's
start date or evidence of a new incident. Neither "known" nor a queued fix stopped incoming reports.
Check new arrivals against tenant configuration and symptoms; recompute counts on each fresh export.

## Triage from now on

The [old subject-only rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) and accepted decision 0001 remain historical
records, not reliable evidence that two reports have the same cause. The replacement
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) explains the new policy.

<DedupeExplorer />

Matching subjects can hide different causes; different subjects can describe the same one.
Look up the tenant locale and booking form, read the channel and body, then merge only
when the cause agrees. Unknown tenants need investigation, not an automatic merge.
Review page dates and computed views before relying on older prose.

